 Similar to [Black](https://black.readthedocs.io/en/stable/the_black_code_style/future_style.html#preview-style), Ruff implements formatting changes
 under the [`preview`](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/settings/#format_preview) flag, promoting them to stable through minor releases, in accordance with our [versioning policy](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/discussions/6998#discussioncomment-7016766).
 
+#### Fluent call chains break before the first call
+
+When a call chain is formatted in fluent style, the preview style now breaks the chain before its
+first call or subscript rather than before the second one. For example:
+
+```python
+# Input
+x = df.merge().groupby().agg().filter()
+
+# Stable
+x = (
+    df.merge()
+    .groupby()
+    .agg()
+    .filter()
+)
+
+# Preview
+x = (
+    df
+    .merge()
+    .groupby()
+    .agg()
+    .filter()
+)
+```
+
+Consecutive calls and subscripts on a single object are treated as one unit when deciding where
+the chain starts. A parenthesized root also counts toward the chain, so a chain with a
+parenthesized root can be split after just one call or subscript.
+
+This change only applies when the [`preview`](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/settings/#format_preview)
+flag is enabled; stable formatting is unchanged.
+
 ### F-string formatting
 
 _Stabilized in Ruff 0.9.0_
